  "solution": {
    "approach": "The problem only asks for the length of the given string S. N is irrelevant. For each test case we read and discard N, then read S and output S.length(). This runs in O(total number of characters) time and O(1) extra space.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(total length of all strings) overall, O(|S|) per test case.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) besides the input string storage.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();\n        int T = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) {\n            br.readLine(); // ignore N\n            String s = br.readLine();\n            out.append(s.length());\n            if (t < T - 1) out.append('\\n');\n        }\n        System.out.print(out.toString());\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
